## Problem

The orchestrator uses a CallbackManager abstraction with CallbackIDs, registration, and unregistration, but:
- Only ever has 2-3 callbacks registered (internal + user)
- CallbackIDs are never actually used for selective unregistration
- Adds indirection without clear benefit

Location: pkg/orchestrator/callbacks.go (inferred from usage)

## Impact

- Over-engineered for current needs
- Makes code harder to follow (callbacks wrapped in callbacks)
- No clear use case for dynamic registration/unregistration

## Suggested Fix

Simplify to direct callback invocation:

```go
type Orchestrator struct {
    internalCallbacks *EventCallbacks
    userCallbacks     *EventCallbacks
    // ... other fields
}

func (o *Orchestrator) invokeCallbacks(event) {
    if o.internalCallbacks != nil {
        o.internalCallbacks.Handle(event)
    }
    if o.userCallbacks != nil {
        o.userCallbacks.Handle(event)
    }
}
```

