## Problem

Tasks are marked as 'Done' even when zero commits are created. The processor only checks `len(mergeResult.Errors) > 0` but doesn't verify that actual work was committed.

## Root Cause

In `pkg/mergequeue/processor.go` lines 211-228:

```go
if len(mergeResult.Errors) > 0 {
    // ... fail the task ...
}
// Mark task as done only if there were no errors
p.markTaskDone(taskID)  // ← Called even if CommitsApplied=0!
```

## Scenarios Where This Happens

1. Agent makes no file changes (`result.Changes` empty)
2. All file changes are filtered out (.beads, .canopy, whiteouts, etc.)
3. Agent creates commits but git am silently fails
4. Files staged but `git diff --cached --quiet` returns 0 (race condition?)

## Observed Behavior

- canopy run completes
- Tasks marked as 'Closed' (successful)
- git log shows NO new commits
- git status shows clean working tree

## Solution

Add validation in processor.go:

```go
// Verify actual work was done
if mergeResult.CommitsApplied == 0 && len(mergeResult.Applied) == 0 {
    // No commits and no file changes applied - this is suspicious
    if p.verbose {
        fmt.Printf("[%s] Warning: merge completed but no changes applied\n", taskID)
    }
    // Either fail the task or at least log a warning
}
```

